    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "BSTIterator it = new BSTIterator([7, 3, 15, null, null, 9, 20])\nit.next()     ->  3\nit.next()     ->  7\nit.hasNext()  ->  true\nit.next()     ->  9\nit.next()     ->  15\nit.next()     ->  20\nit.hasNext()  ->  false"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Flatten in the constructor"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Do the whole in-order walk up front into a list, then hand values out with an index."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n  constructor(root) {\n    this.values = [];\n    this.i = 0;\n    const inorder = (node) => {\n      if (node === null) return;\n      inorder(node.left);\n      this.values.push(node.val);\n      inorder(node.right);\n    };\n    inorder(root);\n  }\n\n  next() {\n    return this.values[this.i++];\n  }\n\n  hasNext() {\n    return this.i < this.values.length;\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "class BSTIterator:\n    def __init__(self, root):\n        self.values = []\n        self.i = 0\n\n        def inorder(node):\n            if node is None:\n                return\n            inorder(node.left)\n            self.values.append(node.val)\n            inorder(node.right)\n\n        inorder(root)\n\n    def next(self):\n        self.i += 1\n        return self.values[self.i - 1]\n\n    def hasNext(self):\n        return self.i < len(self.values)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n    private final List<Integer> values = new ArrayList<>();\n    private int i = 0;\n\n    BSTIterator(TreeNode root) {\n        inorder(root);\n    }\n\n    private void inorder(TreeNode node) {\n        if (node == null) return;\n        inorder(node.left);\n        values.add(node.val);\n        inorder(node.right);\n    }\n\n    int next() {\n        return values.get(i++);\n    }\n\n    boolean hasNext() {\n        return i < values.size();\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n    vector<int> values;\n    size_t i = 0;\n\n    void inorder(TreeNode* node) {\n        if (node == nullptr) return;\n        inorder(node->left);\n        values.push_back(node->val);\n        inorder(node->right);\n    }\n\npublic:\n    BSTIterator(TreeNode* root) {\n        inorder(root);\n    }\n\n    int next() {\n        return values[i++];\n    }\n\n    bool hasNext() {\n        return i < values.size();\n    }\n};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**O(n) constructor, O(1) next and hasNext, O(n) memory.** Fast, but it fails the memory follow-up — and it does all the work even if the caller only wants the first value."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. A stack of the left spine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Unroll the iterative in-order walk and pause it between values. The stack holds the nodes whose left side is done but which haven't been returned yet. `next()` pops the top (the smallest left), then pushes the left spine of its right child."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "bst-iterator",
      "caption": "next() pops the smallest pending node, then pushes the left spine of its right child."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n  constructor(root) {\n    this.stack = [];\n    this.pushLeft(root);\n  }\n\n  pushLeft(node) {                         // the node and its whole left spine\n    while (node !== null) {\n      this.stack.push(node);\n      node = node.left;\n    }\n  }\n\n  next() {\n    const node = this.stack.pop();         // the smallest value not yet returned\n    this.pushLeft(node.right);             // its right subtree comes next\n    return node.val;\n  }\n\n  hasNext() {\n    return this.stack.length > 0;\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "class BSTIterator:\n    def __init__(self, root):\n        self.stack = []\n        self.push_left(root)\n\n    def push_left(self, node):            # the node and its whole left spine\n        while node is not None:\n            self.stack.append(node)\n            node = node.left\n\n    def next(self):\n        node = self.stack.pop()           # the smallest value not yet returned\n        self.push_left(node.right)        # its right subtree comes next\n        return node.val\n\n    def hasNext(self):\n        return len(self.stack) > 0"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n    private final Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();\n\n    BSTIterator(TreeNode root) {\n        pushLeft(root);\n    }\n\n    private void pushLeft(TreeNode node) {           // the node and its whole left spine\n        while (node != null) {\n            stack.push(node);\n            node = node.left;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int next() {\n        TreeNode node = stack.pop();                 // the smallest value not yet returned\n        pushLeft(node.right);                        // its right subtree comes next\n        return node.val;\n    }\n\n    boolean hasNext() {\n        return !stack.isEmpty();\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "class BSTIterator {\n    stack<TreeNode*> st;\n\n    void pushLeft(TreeNode* node) {                  // the node and its whole left spine\n        while (node != nullptr) {\n            st.push(node);\n            node = node->left;\n        }\n    }\n\npublic:\n    BSTIterator(TreeNode* root) {\n        pushLeft(root);\n    }\n\n    int next() {\n        TreeNode* node = st.top();                   // the smallest value not yet returned\n        st.pop();\n        pushLeft(node->right);                       // its right subtree comes next\n        return node->val;\n    }\n\n    bool hasNext() {\n        return !st.empty();\n    }\n};"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**O(h) memory, O(1) amortized time.** One `next()` may push a long spine, but every node is pushed once and popped once over the whole iteration — n pushes spread over n calls."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Flatten in the constructor",
          "time": "O(1) per call",
          "timeWhy": "The constructor does **O(n)** up front; then `next` just reads the next list item.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The list holds **every value** in the tree."
        },
        {
          "approach": "A stack of the left spine",
          "time": "O(1) amortized",
          "timeWhy": "Each node is **pushed once and popped once** over the whole iteration: n pushes spread over n calls.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The stack holds **one path** down the tree."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**A single node** — one next(), then hasNext() is false.",
        "**A chain going left** — the constructor pushes all n nodes; later calls push nothing.",
        "**A chain going right** — the stack never holds more than one node.",
        "**hasNext() called several times in a row** — it must not move the iterator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Reverse iterator (largest first)** — push the right spine and step into left children.",
        "**BST Iterator II (prev and next)** — keep a list of returned values plus the stack.",
        "**Two Sum IV in O(h) space** — one forward and one reverse iterator act as the two pointers.",
        "**Peeking iterator** — remember the next value before it's asked for."
      ]
    }
  ],
